    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21164" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hypăta</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὑπάτη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small town of
				Thessaly</i>, <i>near the Penēus</i>,
			now <i>Neópatra</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 36,
				16, 4</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hypătaei</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>its
				inhabitants</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 36, 14</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exsules,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					41, 25, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
